 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "Your family needs a place to hide if the worst ever happens.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you bury a shipping container in the backyard. Problem solved!",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But a container is only strong at its corners, and the dirt crushes the roof.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you bury a round steel tube instead. The curve spreads the weight.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But fallout lands right on top, and a foot of dirt barely slows the radiation.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you pile on three feet of earth. Every three and a half inches halves it.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But your hatch goes straight down, and so does the radiation.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you give the entrance a ninety degree turn. Radiation flies straight, so it hits the wall.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then, after a day inside, the air gets hot, wet and stale.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you add a hand pump that pulls fresh air in and pushes stale air out.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Congratulations! You just built a nuclear bunker. What should we build next?",
   "pausa": 0.2
  }
 ],
